From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ricardo Pardini <ricardo@pardini.net>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 21:13:40 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] arm: mediatek: mt8195: get DRAM size from TF-A boot argument

Genio 1200 boards (eg. Radxa NIO-12L) come in several DRAM sizes
(4/8/16 GiB) while sharing a single devicetree. The (vendor) TF-A BL2,
after libdram initializes the memory, stores the actual size in a small
boot argument structure at a fixed DRAM location (0x40000100).

Use it when present, falling back to the devicetree memory node
otherwise. Also make the DDR mem_map entry follow the detected size, so
16 GiB boards are fully mapped (the Kconfig default covers 8 GiB) and
smaller boards don't map nonexistent memory.

The kernel devicetree memory node is already fixed up from gd->dram[]
by arch_fixup_fdt(), so the OS gets the correct size too.

Based on work by Bartosz Bilas <b.bilas@grinn-global.com> for mt8188.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: Ricardo Pardini <ricardo@pardini.net>
---
 arch/arm/include/asm/arch-mediatek/misc.h | 21 +++++++++++++++++++
 arch/arm/mach-mediatek/mt8195/init.c      | 25 ++++++++++++++++++++++-
 2 files changed, 45 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm/include/asm/arch-mediatek/misc.h b/arch/arm/include/asm/arch-mediatek/misc.h
index 2530e78a5f1..c8d456f80af 100644
--- a/arch/arm/include/asm/arch-mediatek/misc.h
+++ b/arch/arm/include/asm/arch-mediatek/misc.h
@@ -14,4 +14,25 @@
 #define APHW_VER		0x08
 #define APSW_VER		0x0c
 
+/*
+ * Boot argument passed by (vendor) TF-A BL2 to BL33, at a fixed location in
+ * DRAM, after libdram has initialized and sized the memory. This is not the
+ * legacy preloader boot argument (see mt7623/preloader.h); only the magic
+ * value happens to be the same.
+ */
+#define MTK_TFA_BOOT_ARG_LOCATION	0x40000100
+#define MTK_TFA_BOOT_ARG_MAGIC		0x504c504c
+
+#ifndef __ASSEMBLY__
+#include <linux/types.h>
+
+struct mtk_tfa_boot_arg {
+	u32 magic_number;
+	u64 dram_size;
+};
+
+#define MTK_TFA_BOOT_ARG \
+	((struct mtk_tfa_boot_arg *)MTK_TFA_BOOT_ARG_LOCATION)
+#endif
+
 #endif /* __MEDIATEK_MISC_H_ */
diff --git a/arch/arm/mach-mediatek/mt8195/init.c b/arch/arm/mach-mediatek/mt8195/init.c
index 6afb7330b4e..6f4cdb2c05a 100644
--- a/arch/arm/mach-mediatek/mt8195/init.c
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-mediatek/mt8195/init.c
@@ -6,6 +6,7 @@
  *         Chris-QJ Chen <chris-qj.chen@mediatek.com>
  */
 
+#include <asm/arch/misc.h>
 #include <asm/armv8/mmu.h>
 #include <asm/system.h>
 #include <dm/uclass.h>
@@ -17,7 +18,29 @@ DECLARE_GLOBAL_DATA_PTR;
 
 int dram_init(void)
 {
-	return fdtdec_setup_mem_size_base();
+	struct mtk_tfa_boot_arg *arg = MTK_TFA_BOOT_ARG;
+	int ret;
+
+	/*
+	 * The DRAM size depends on the board variant (eg 4/8/16 GiB); TF-A BL2
+	 * (with libdram) knows the actual size and passes it in a boot
+	 * argument. Fall back to the devicetree if it is not there.
+	 */
+	if (arg->magic_number == MTK_TFA_BOOT_ARG_MAGIC && arg->dram_size) {
+		gd->ram_base = CONFIG_MTK_MEM_MAP_DDR_BASE_PHY;
+		gd->ram_size = arg->dram_size;
+	} else {
+		ret = fdtdec_setup_mem_size_base();
+		if (ret)
+			return ret;
+	}
+
+	/* Map exactly the available DRAM, which might exceed the Kconfig default */
+	mem_map[0].virt = gd->ram_base;
+	mem_map[0].phys = gd->ram_base;
+	mem_map[0].size = gd->ram_size;
+
+	return 0;
 }
 
 phys_addr_t board_get_usable_ram_top(phys_size_t total_size)
